      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t understand this distinction well. The only function with this convention is `enforce_pd_chipset_resume_policy`, and it is only called when the power state is \"on.\" I think the main important thing about this function is that it needs to be called before `enforce_pd_chipset_on_state_policy`, but at least at the call site, nothing indicates that we are actually resuming at this time.",
