      "writtenOn": "2025-02-10T21:35:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The names seem a little unintuitive in this case. The power state is \"on,\" so we\u0027re calling the suspend  policy, then the on policy, then the resume policy? That seems surprising to me. In the previous code, there were two functions that did the same thing, but their names expressed their different purpose, albeit vaguely.\n\n@asemjonovs@google.com @honscheid@google.com @keithshort@chromium.org Do you have any ideas for how to most clearly describe the power-state transition policies? This is something we\u0027ve punted on up to this point.",
      "revId": "32275e20f4548e4328c8a1918c94e3d1290b115a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "abb45103_25eb78da",
