      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-11T02:22:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My suggestion would be to name it similar to the chip state we are in.  In this case `CHIPSET_STATE_ON` so `enforce_pd_chipset_on_policy`.  \nI never quite understood why we call three `enforce_*` APIs here (as there\u0027s no thread context switching occurring to handle these individually) when I think it should be just one, which sets up the final state of `(src|snk)_policy.accept_power_role_swap` and `una_policy.(cc_mode|flags)` after all these have been called.",
      "parentUuid": "1058995b_7b0dd538",
